{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1557974210,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWU0NDQ3MjY2NDM=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3424","origin":"github"},"title":"publish: should report that not all requested data was published since not present locally","message":"#### What is the problem?\n\nMay be it was an evening prior time as well, but I now recall myself in the same WTF state trying to publish all data for a dataset to a remote and getting nothing there... First I did setup `annex wanted` and just used `datalad publish`. Then tried with specifying paths, with direct `git-annex copy --to ... *` invocation (which also was not informative) to only later realize -- \"khe khe -- you old fool have no data locally since you initially forgot to `install -g` it!\".\n\nSo, while for the ongoing \"publish overhaul\" of @mih project - it would be nice if there was some kind of an indication that not all data pointed by the paths was actually copied simply because there is no data for them even locally.\n\nIt is not a priority issue but having burnt myself twice already, I guess I could hit it again ;-)","files":null}]}